e\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> numbers exactly\nonce."},"p:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_correct":{"href":"../lax-470956/Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_correct.html","incident":["e:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_correct:conclusion:Lax470956.Construction1.reduce_correct:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"On a word that is a graph the claim is the correctness of Construction 1, transported\nalong the encoding on the right and along the choice of instance on the left; on any\nother word both sides are false, the left because there is no graph and the right\nbecause the word the map emits has a job it cannot run.","nodeId":"p:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_correct","semanticId":"Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_correct","tooltipHtml":"On a word that is a graph the claim is the correctness of Construction 1, transported\nalong the encoding on the right and along the choice of instance on the left; on any\nother word both sides are false, the left because there is no graph and the right\nbecause the word the map emits has a job it cannot run."},"p:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_maps":{"href":"../lax-470956/Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_maps.html","incident":["e:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_maps:conclusion:Lax470956.Construction1.reduce_maps:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Either the map emits Construction 1's word, which presents the constructed instance and\nits threshold, or it emits the fixed word, which presents one job and the threshold one.","nodeId":"p:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_maps","semanticId":"Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_maps","tooltipHtml":"Either the map emits Construction 1's word, which presents the constructed instance and\nits threshold, or it emits the fixed word, which presents one job and the threshold one."},"p:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_param":{"href":"../lax-470956/Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_param.html","incident":["e:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_param:conclusion:Lax470956.Construction1.reduce_param:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The constructed instance has one machine for each pair of colours and one more, and the\nnumber of colours is the last entry of the word; so the parameter of the image is a\nfunction of the parameter of the source alone. An unrecognized word is sent to a word\nwith no machine at all.","nodeId":"p:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_param","semanticId":"Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Reduce.reduce_param","tooltipHtml":"The constructed instance has one machine for each pair of colours and one more, and the\nnumber of colours is the last entry of the word; so the parameter of the image is a\nfunction of the parameter of the source alone. An unrecognized word is sent to a word\nwith no machine at all."},"p:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Renum.correct":{"href":"../lax-470956/Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Renum.correct.html","incident":["e:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Renum.correct:conclusion:Lax470956.Construction1.correct:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Section 3 of the paper, joined to the archive's shapes.\n\nThe argument itself — Observation 3, Lemma 1 and Lemma 2 — is the paper's, proved over\nthe paper's own presentation: an abstract finite vertex type, and jobs and machines named\nstructurally as sums and subtypes. Three translations carry it to the numbered instance\nthe concept builds. `ofInstance` is the instance shape, and on it the two notions of\nmulticoloured clique are the same proposition. `ord` is the order `<π`, which\nthe paper assumes exists and the concept fixes by ranking vertices by colour and breaking\nties by index. And `renum` is the numbering: the machines correspond exactly, the jobs\nembed, and the slots outside that embedding carry inert jobs — weight zero and no\neligible machine at all, so feasibility alone forces a schedule to reject them and they\nchange neither side.\n\nThe padding is the cost of indexing by all ordered pairs. A closed-form job index is two\ndivisions, where enumerating only the edges of the graph would be a search; the cost is\n`n²` edge slots of which only the edges are jobs, and `Renumbering.hasWeight_iff` is\nwhere it is paid.","nodeId":"p:Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Renum.correct","semanticId":"Lax470956Proofs.Construction1Renum.correct","tooltipHtml":"Section 3 of the paper, joined to the archive's shapes.\n\nThe argument itself — Observation 3, Lemma 1 and Lemma 2 — is the paper's, proved over\nthe paper's own presentation: an abstract finite vertex type, and jobs and machines named\nstructurally as sums and subtypes. Three translations carry it to the numbered instance\nthe concept builds. <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ofInstance</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">o</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">an</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ce</span></span></span></span> is the instance shape, and on it the two notions of\nmulticoloured clique are the same proposition. <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ord</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">or</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span></span></span></span> is the order <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">&lt;π</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span></span></span></span>, which\nthe paper assumes exists and the concept fixes by ranking vertices by colour and breaking\nties by index. And <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">renum</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span></span></span></span> is the numbering: the machines correspond exactly, the jobs\nembed, and the slots outside that embedding carry inert jobs — weight zero and no\neligible machine at all, so feasibility alone forces a schedule to reject them and they\nchange neither side.\n\nThe padding is the cost of indexing by all ordered pairs. A closed-form job index is two\ndivisions, where enumerating only the edges of the graph would be a search; the cost is\n<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n²</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> edge slots of which only the edges are jobs, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Renumbering.hasWeight_iff</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mord mathnorma